# No AI (AI Policy)

Since LLM/AI tools are part of our reality for quite a while already,
here is my AI policy:

**I don't use LLMs for writing**. Neither in this blog, nor in other
written personal or work forms. Writing is about communication.
Communication is about trust. If you recieve ideas/messages/email from me -
it was not composed or edited by LLM.

I might use LLMs for generating some parts of the description or
fact-based tables but those parts will always be marked as AI-generated.

I might use LLMs for fixing grammar in the future. I think it's a valid
and useful case. However, I'm not sure if it might push me to the slippery
slope so I'm still hesitating to do it personally. But this might change.

If you are texting me - please consider writing it by yourself even if your
writing skills are not that fancy comparing to some GPT-3000-Universe
(or whatever version is out there). Send me ideas composed in your voice.
Or just mark generated content. I would really appreciate that. Otherwise
I'm not sure I want to read what you put very little effort writing.

